/E (Part B implements a 4-bit barrel shifter that performs a circular right rotation. Unlike the single-position shifter, no bits are lost during rotation. Instead, the bit shifted out from the least significant position re-enters at the most significant position.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [10]
